    {
     "text": "```python\nfrom pedantic import trace_class\n\n@trace_class\nclass Perceptron:\n    \"\"\"\n    A Perceptron is a type of linear classifier used in machine learning.\n    It is a single-layer neural network that makes predictions based on a linear combination of input features.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, input_size, learning_rate=0.01, iterations=1000):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the Perceptron with given input size, learning rate, and number of iterations.\n\n        Args:\n            input_size (int): The number of input features.\n            learning_rate (float): The step size used to update weights during training.\n            iterations (int): The number of training iterations to perform.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.weights = [0.0] * input_size\n        self.bias = 0.0\n        self.learning_rate = learning_rate\n        self.iterations = iterations\n\n    def train(self, features, labels):\n        \"\"\"\n        Train the Perceptron using the provided features and labels.\n\n        Args:\n            features (list of lists): A list of input feature vectors.\n            labels (list of floats): A list of target labels (0 or 1).\n        \"\"\"\n        for _ in range(self.iterations):\n            for feature, label in zip(features, labels):\n                prediction = self._predict(feature)\n                error = label - prediction\n                self.weights = [w + self.learning_rate * error * feature[i] for i, w in enumerate(self.weights)]\n                self.bias += self.learning_rate * error\n\n    def _predict(self, feature):\n        \"\"\"\n        Predict the class label for a given feature vector.\n\n        Args:\n            feature (list of floats): A list of input feature values.\n\n        Returns:\n            float: The predicted label (0 or 1).\n        \"\"\"\n        return 1.0 if sum(w * f for w, f in zip(self.weights, feature)) + self.bias >= 0 else 0.0\n\n    def predict(self, features):\n        \"\"\"\n        Predict the class labels for a list of feature vectors.\n\n        Args:\n            features (list of lists): A list of input feature vectors.\n\n        Returns:\n            list of floats: A list of predicted labels (0 or 1).\n        \"\"\"\n        return [self._predict(feature) for feature in features]\n```",
